SUMMARY:Gospel Music Festival
DESCRIPTION:Gospel Music Festival\nDecember 12 at 5:00 p.m.\nMain Stage at Union County Performing Arts Center\nFREE admission\nClick HERE for tickets \nJoin us for an unforgettable evening of inspiration\, hope\, and celebration at the Gospel Music Festival. The concert opens with Elevation\, Delaware’s only professional vocal ensemble\, under the direction of Dr. Arreon A. Harley-Emerson\, whose innovative performances blend classical choral music with jazz\, hip-hop\, R&B\, storytelling\, and spoken word. In the second half\, the New Jersey Youth Symphony and distinguished high school choruses from across New Jersey\, under the baton of Helen H. Cha-Pyo\, present André J. Thomas’s uplifting Mass: A Celebration of Love and Joy\, a powerful work that celebrates faith\, unity\, hope\, and the transformative power of music. \nNew Jersey Youth Symphony Helen H. Cha-Pyo\, Music Director & Conductor\nElevation Dr. Arreon A. Harley-Emerson\, Artistic Director\nJ.P. Stevens High School Chorus Matthew Chi Lee & Regina McElroy\, Directors\nSomerville High School Chorus Daniel Malloy\, Director\nRosa Parks High School for the Arts Chorus Lauren Sander-Wells\, Director \nThis concert is part of the Wharton Arts Free Concert Series at UCPAC\, offering six free performances that celebrate music\, culture\, and community throughout the season. \n \nSupported by funding through the NJEDA‘s A.R.T. – Phase II Grant Program.
URL:https://whartonarts.org/calendar/gospel-music-festival/
LOCATION:Union County Performing Arts Center in Rahway\, 1601 Irving St\, Rahway\, New Jersey\, 07065\, United States
CATEGORIES:NJYS,NJYS Alumni,Wharton
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://whartonarts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/NJEDA-Dec-12-5pm-Cal.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="NJYS":MAILTO:info@NJYS.org
END:VEVENT
