LAST-MODIFIED:20260918T193711Z
UID:10000471-1797170400-1797175800@whartonarts.org
SUMMARY:Two Nutcrackers
DESCRIPTION:Two Nutcrackers \nDecember 13 at 2:00 pm\nMain Stage at the Union County Performing Arts Center\nFREE Admission\nClick HERE for tickets \nExperience a holiday tradition like you’ve never heard before! Two Nutcrackers brings together two unforgettable interpretations of the beloved classic\, featuring the timeless elegance of Tchaikovsky’s The Nutcracker Suite alongside the vibrant jazz reimagining of Duke Ellington and Billy Strayhorn’s The Nutcracker Suite. This festive concert celebrates the magic of the season through the rich traditions of both classical and jazz music\, offering audiences two distinct musical journeys inspired by the same timeless story. The concert opens with the NJYS Youth Orchestra\, performing works by Coleridge-Taylor\, Rachmaninoff\, Humperdinck\, and more. \nNJYS Youth Orchestra Oliver Hagen\, Conductor\nNJYS Jazz Orchestra Shamie Royston\, Director\nNJYS Youth Symphony Helen H. Cha-Pyo\, Music Director & Conductor \nThis concert is part of the Wharton Arts Free Concert Series at UCPAC\, offering six free performances that celebrate music\, culture\, and community throughout the season. \n \nSupported by funding through the NJEDA‘s A.R.T. – Phase II Grant Program.
URL:https://whartonarts.org/calendar/two-nutcrackers/
LOCATION:Union County Performing Arts Center in Rahway\, 1601 Irving St\, Rahway\, New Jersey\, 07065\, United States
CATEGORIES:NJYS,NJYS Alumni,Wharton
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://whartonarts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/NJEDA-Dec-13-2pm-cal.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="NJYS":MAILTO:info@NJYS.org
END:VEVENT
